(a) Sale of impounded property. The owner of any property impounded under the provisions of this article shall have 30 days from the date the same was impounded to redeem the same by paying the cost of removal and storage. After 30 days from the date of the impounding of any property under the terms hereof, the chief of police, or his designee, may sell or otherwise dispose of the same in accordance with the procedures in O.C.G.A. § 9-13-140 et seq. and after giving opportunity for competitive bidding.
